{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429127-skinstealing","id":429127,"title":"Skinstealing","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-05T12:17:23-08:00","id":429127,"title":"Skinstealing","content":"So, up front: I like the new Skin Thief facet. It cuts way down on the absurd logistical ease of old skinstealing and makes it a lot more...I don't know the right word. Genre? Primal? It's more fitting to a game about savage fury.<br /> <br /> That said, this is a thread about houseruling it and playing around with gift-making to go about it a third way. I want to play with making the logistics a little easier, and throw in some of the other deceptive powers from first edition, and then made up a thing.<br /> <br /> I thought about modeling this as a wolf gift but that seems too cheap, so call this a shadow gift. There's fluff to be played with - you probably learn this from<i> interesting </i>spirits - and details, and probably renaming, but this is a first draft to get my thoughts down. You'd also probably want to replace the cunning facet of the Gift of Change but I haven't sorted that one quite yet.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Gift of Skinstealing</span></b><br /> <br /> <b>Skin Thief (Cunning)</b><br /> <br /> The Uratha steals the shape and look of their prey.<br /> <br /> Cost: 2 Essence<br /> Action: Instant<br /> Duration: Special<br /> <br /> The Uratha may take the shape of any human or animal who she has tasted the blood of and brought down in the <i>Siskur-Dah</i> within the past week. An animal must be roughly wolf-sized and predatory. If this is done solely to obtain a shape, and there is not another reason for the hunt, it is a breaking point towards Flesh.<br /> <br /> Once she has paid the Essence cost of the Facet and entered the appropriate form (hishu or urhan), the Uratha warps and ripples for a few seconds and settles into a perfect physical copy of the prey. The mimicry lasts until she willingly sheds the stolen shape or shapeshifts, bloodily tearing her way out of the false sheath. She can avoid this tearing by spending an additional instant action to shapeshift on top of what she normally requires and spends a willpower point, in which case it becomes the 'default' appearance to which Hishu or Urhan reverts. Once it has been a week since the Uratha finished obtaining her taste and dominance of the prey, the skin crumbles to dust.<br /> <br /> Without use of the Spoor Thief facet, the Uratha's scent is a strange mix of their own and their prey's, clearly distinct from either and with recognizable parts of both (though it favors the prey). Without use of the Song Thief facet, it also makes no change to the Uratha's voice. No facet enables the Uratha to steal the look of their prey's eyes.<br /> <br /> <b>Song Thief (Glory)</b><br /> <br /> The Uratha flawlessly imitates the voice of a creature it has hunted - or a voice its prey wants to hear.<br /> <br /> Cost: 1 Essence<br /> Dice Pool: Wits + Expression + Glory (-Composure)<br /> Action: Instant<br /> Duration: One scene<br /> <br /> This power may be targeted against an individual the Uratha can perceive, in which case their Composure is subtracted from the activation pool. The Uratha may choose to steal either a feared voice or a desired voice, and will have an intuitive understanding of who they are imitating, but has no exact control over who they 'become.'<br /> <br /> If the target is a known subject of the Uratha's <i>Siskur-Dah</i>, the power may be used over the phone (or Skype).<br /> <br /> Alternately, the Uratha may take the voice of any human or animal who they she has listened to and then somehow silenced within the past week. This could by exhausting them, punching them in the throat or gut, kissing them mid-sentence, or killing them, among other methods. Some sneak next to the sleeping and steal their breath for a few moments.<br /> <br /> <b>Roll Results</b><br /> Dramatic Failure: The Uratha's voice gets jumbled up for a scene, different voices overlapping and contradicting each other and sometimes speaking in tongues. They must succeed at a Presence + Expression - Glory roll to convey even simple concepts<br /> Failure: The Uratha can't mimic the voice.<br /> Success: The Uratha perfectly steals the voice. In addition to whatever ends they might put it to, this improves their impression for appropriate social influences by one step.<br /> Exceptional Success: The Uratha may switch back and forth between their own voice and the stolen voice at will, and takes [Glory] extra dice on social rolls to deceive and persuade using the facet to their advantage.<br /> <br /> <b>Patient Thief (Honor)</b><br /> <br /> This enhances uses of other facets of the gift. It allows the character to reflexively re-pay activation costs to seamlessly extend the duration of their powers, and the time between obtaining their piece of a victim and imitating them can be up to one month instead of one week.<br /> <br /> <b>Spoor Thief (Purity)</b><br /> <br /> Many of the Uratha will believe their noses before their eyes. This facet lets them be deceived as easily as the scent-blind.<br /> <br /> Cost: 1 Essence<br /> Dice Pool: Stamina + Subterfuge + Purity<br /> Action: Instant<br /> Duration: One scene<br /> <br /> The Uratha may perfectly imitate the scent of any human or animal who he has tracked for at least one scene and tasted a fluid other than blood from - sweat, piss, semen, or spit, for example - within the past week. This does not require a roll.<br /> <br /> Additionally (or alternately), the Uratha may twist their scent to seem healthy, wounded, diseased, or convey any other scent-born lies, which <i>does</i> require a roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Roll Results</b><br /> Dramatic Failure: The Uratha is pretty sure he's got the scent imitated perfectly!<br /> Failure: The Uratha fails to change his scent.<br /> Success: The Uratha changes his scent perfectly.<br /> Exceptional Success: The Uratha may apply [Purity] as a penalty to any rolls contesting deception enabled by the Uratha's disguise.<br /> <br /> <b>Head Thief (Wisdom)</b><br /> <br /> A wise Uratha is not limited to riding beasts and machines.<br /> <br /> Cost: 2 Essence<br /> Dice Pool: Manipulation + Intimidation + Wisdom - Resolve<br /> Action: Instant<br /> Duration: One scene<br /> <br /> This power may be used on any human the Uratha has observed for at least one scene and then stolen hair from within the past week. The Uratha must be able to see the individual again and swallow the hair to activate the facet.<br /> <br /> <b>Roll Results</b><br /> Dramatic Failure: Distracted by glimpses of another mind but completely unable to understand it, the Uratha suffers from the Madness condition for the rest of the scene and may not try to activate the Facet again.<br /> Failure: The Uratha fails to activate the Facet.<br /> Success: The Uratha\u2019s mind rides the individual for as long as she wishes, immersing her senses in those of her target. She can let them do as they like, or take direct control (whereupon the target blacks out). While riding, she cannot perceive with her own senses at all and appears to be in a state of deep sleep. Returning to her own senses takes an instant action and ends the Facet. Should the human be killed while she is riding, she is ejected back to her own body and treats it as a breaking point towards Spirit. Should the Uratha be slain while she is riding, a fragment of her spirit becomes subsumed into the target, creating a strange Claimed.<br /> Exceptional Success: The Uratha remains somewhat aware of her own surroundings and is alerted if her real body is injured.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T13:56:28-08:00","id":429278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429127-skinstealing#post429127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once she has paid the Essence cost of the Facet and entered the appropriate form (hishu or urhan), the Uratha warps and ripples for a few seconds and settles into a perfect physical copy of the prey. The mimicry lasts until she willingly sheds the stolen shape or shapeshifts, bloodily tearing her way out of the false sheath. She can avoid this tearing by spending an additional instant action to shapeshift on top of what she normally requires and spends a willpower point, in which case it becomes the 'default' appearance to which Hishu or Urhan reverts.</div> </div> </div> </div>This would be the thing I'd take from it. I'd like it if the urhan shifting being able to last was also available for the hishu form.<br /> <br /> I also like Head Thief a lot, though I find the direct control a bit too powerful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}